{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>And this shall be the sign for you.</b> That is, this will be the sign — that they shall serve Elohim on this mountain when they go out from Egypt. And then I will make it known to all that I sent you, as it is written at the giving of the Torah: ״ויאמר ה' אל משה הנה אנכי בא אליך בעב הענן בעבור ישמע העם וידעו כי אתה שלוחי״. Another explanation: <b>and this shall be the sign for you</b> is turned back upon what Moses said: ״מי אנכי כי אלך״ — that is, I am not worthy to speak to the kingdom. And even if I am worthy of this, am I worthy to bring Israel out of Egypt? The Holy One, blessed be He, said to him: כי אהיה על ידך — that is, if through Me, כי אהיה עמך in that mission. <b>And this shall be the sign for you</b> that I will be with you: כי אנכי שלחתיך — and since I sent you, you must know that I will not abandon you in My mission to help you. From Rabbi David, who heard it from Rabbi Joseph Kara."], :book :exodus, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:02:36.532980872Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}